  "notes": "The 2008–2012 anthem era, and the kick is the whole argument: four on the floor every bar, never the parent's sparse 1-and-and-of-2. Claps and snaps stacked on the 2 and 4, offbeat open hats sitting on every & over straight 8th closed hats, and a bass that walks the offbeat eighths so the pump is in the notes rather than only in the mix. Major keys and the four-chord axis, a chorus melody written high and sung loud, and a snare-roll ladder eight bars out — where house takes the same floor into minor sevenths, this takes it into a stadium. ⚠ **`drums.kick.lockTo808` removed (2026-08-17, 808 gate).** This kit authors `bass808: null` — it has no 808 — and `lockTo808` is the one parameter that says *how much of the kick the 808 follows*, so here it described a pairing that does not exist: `generators::drums::bass808` returns on `block.is_none()` before the value is ever read, which makes it provably dead in this file. Where it was not dead was in the artists and producers who extend this kit and author an 808 of their OWN: they inherited the zero and `kicks.iter().filter(|_| rng.random_bool(0.0))` kept nothing, so their sub lane was silent at every seed and `bass808::every_shipped_model_with_an_808_produces_a_playable_line` reported \"no 808 at all\". Removing it restores the engine's documented default of 1.0 for exactly those children and changes nothing here. ⚠ No researched claim moved: the entry's own statement about this kit is the `bass808: null` beside it, and that is untouched.",
